TurboSens is a synthetic turbofan degradation dataset generated with \texttt{OpenDeckSMR}, a component‑level thermodynamic simulator that exposes \emph{both} the observable sensor stream and the ground‑truth health state $\mathbf{s}_t$, the key property that enables direct evaluation of learned representations.

We release two scenarios, summarized in Table~\ref{tab:odsmr_base}. \textbf{TurboSens1} reproduces the setting of \cite{REMOVE} in an interactive environment: time‑based maintenance, two actions, and 4 flight contexts. \textbf{TurboSens3} significantly raises the realism: health‑correlated maintenance with six actions, four heterogeneous degradation archetypes, twelve flight contexts, a library of ten stochastic events (bird strike, compressor surge, icing, etc.), and imperfect restoration. Full details of Scenario 3 are provided in Appendix~\ref{sec:dataset_scenario3}.

TurboSens is designed to challenge world models with sparse, imbalanced interventions ($0.04\%$-$0.26\%$ of steps contain maintenance), heterogeneous failure trajectories, and multi‑context partial observability. The dataset is generated on‑demand via a provided script; the reference splits are released as HDF5 files with a documented schema.


\subsection{Datasets Coverage}


\subsubsection{OpenDeckSMR Basic}

It reflects the dataset generated in \cite{REMOVE} but re-implemented in an interactive environment where we can apply actions in real time. This allows a direct comparison with more static methods. 


\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\small
\begin{tabular}{clcl}
\toprule
\textbf{Action} & \textbf{Component (LLP)} & \textbf{HI indices} & \textbf{Effect} \\
\midrule
0 & Idle (no maintenance)    & —       & No state change \\
1 & Fan disk                 & $s_1, s_2$  & Partial restoration of fan HI \\
2 & LPC disk                 & $s_3, s_4$  & Partial restoration of LPC HI \\
3 & HPC disk                 & $s_5, s_6$  & Partial restoration of HPC HI \\
4 & HPT disk                 & $s_7, s_8$  & Partial restoration of HPT HI \\
5 & LPT disk                 & $s_9, s_{10}$ & Partial restoration of LPT HI \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\caption{Life-Limited Part (LLP) replacement actions in TurboSens3.
Each action targets a specific rotating assembly; its HI components are
partially restored upon replacement. Cycle limits and restoration
magnitudes follow OpenDeckSMR component maps.}
\label{tab:llp}
\end{table}

The 0.26\% maintenance rate reflects industrial reality: repair events are scarce, creating a highly imbalanced action distribution that challenges standard sequence models.

\begin{itemize}
    \item Design choices motivated by industrial realism: Multi-context observations: four flight phases per timestep, matching operational data collection practice in aviation health monitoring
    \item Rare maintenance events: the action distribution is heavily skewed, requiring models to learn from sparse intervention signals
    \item Stochastic degradation trajectories: episode-to-episode variability prevents memorization and tests generalization across degradation paths
    \item Physics-motivated failure criterion: episode termination at component-specific bounds, not arbitrary horizons
\end{itemize}

